  "history": {
    "en": "Sircar records 'Shrihatta' (Sylhet) as a variant reading of this pitha's name, and Bengali tradition places it at the Shri Shail Mahalakshmi temple in Jainpur village, Dakshin Surma, about 3 km south-east of Sylhet town in Bangladesh. Other lists identify this pitha with Srisailam in Andhra Pradesh instead, which also has its own entry as the Shriparvata pitha.",
    "hi": "",
    "bn": "",
    "mr": "",
    "ta": "",
    "te": "",
    "gu": ""
  },
  "story": {
    "en": "According to the Puranas, Sati, the daughter of Daksha, gave up her life in the fire of her father's sacrifice after he insulted her husband Shiva. Grieving, Shiva carried her body across the world until Vishnu's discus divided it, and each place where a part fell became a Shakti Peetha. Tradition holds that Sati's neck fell here.",
    "hi": "",
    "bn": "",
    "mr": "",
    "ta": "",
    "te": "",
    "gu": ""
  },
  "facts": {
    "en": [
      "The goddess here is Mahalakshmi and the Bhairava Shambarananda.",
      "The shrine is also called Mahalakshmi Bhairavi Griva Mahapeetha, 'griva' meaning neck.",
      "It is one of the Pithanirnaya's pithas in present-day Bangladesh."
    ],
